{title: He Will Not Sleep}
{subtitle: Psalms 121:4}
{key: D}
{tempo: 69}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Lay your head down, [G]little [D]one
The lamps are [Bm]low, the [A]day is [D]done
The Lord [G]who made the [A]hills and [Bm]sky
Is watch[G]ing you, and so [A]am I
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He [G]will not slumber, he [D]will not sleep
The [Bm]one who keeps you, [A]he will keep
Your go[G]ing out, your [D]com[A/C#]ing [Bm]in
[G]Sleep [A]now, sleep a[D]gain
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The sun won't hurt you [G]through the [D]day
The moon won't [Bm]harm you [A]on your [D]way
The Lord [G]will keep you [A]from all [Bm]harm
As[G]leep with[A]in his [D]arm
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He will not [G]slumber, he will not [D]sleep
The one who [Bm]keeps you, he will [A]keep
Your going [G]out, your com[D]ing [A/C#][Bm]in
[G]Sleep now, [A]sleep a[D]gain
{end_of_chorus}
